      <description><![CDATA[
        Washington draws a hard line on artificial intelligence. The US Department of Homeland Security has officially ordered the removal and procurement ban of China&#39;s DeepSeek across all civilian IT systems, citing severe data transfer and espionage risks.
        
        [SPLIT]
        ⚡ The directive mandates the immediate removal of DeepSeek products and third-party services leveraging the model from all civilian federal networks.
        [SPLIT]
        ⚡ Federal agencies were previously instructed via a July memo to aggressively monitor inbound and outbound traffic flows to isolate DeepSeek signatures.
